    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d153">

                <pb facs="0253" n="147" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg147"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Egan to Mr.
                            Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-07-25"><hi rendition="#italic">July 25,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Egan telegraphs that the English, German, and French ministers have given an
                    undertaking, which the Chilean Government requires as a condition of clearing
                    cargoes from Chilean ports, that if ships should be forcibly compelled to enter
                    ports in control of revolutionists their liberation will be exacted by the
                    fleets of their respective nations. Mr. Egan asks whether he may give the same
                    assurance.</p>
            </div>
